.TH start-cli-backup-volume-restore 1  "restore "
.SH NAME
start\-cli\-backup\-volume\-restore \- Restore volumes as new local copies
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBstart\-cli backup volume restore\fR [\fB\-\-server\-id\fR] [\fB\-\-format\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fITARGET_ID\fR> <\fIPASSWORD\fR> [\fIIDS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Restore volumes as new local copies
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-server\-id\fR \fI<SERVER_ID>\fR
Unique server identifier
.TP
\fB\-\-format\fR

.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fITARGET_ID\fR>
Backup target identifier
.TP
<\fIPASSWORD\fR>
Password for backup encryption
.TP
[\fIIDS\fR]
Volume backup IDs to restore as new local volumes
